  "known_limitations": [
    "CLIP and DINOv2 are general-purpose pretrained encoders, not conservation-specific semantic judges.",
    "Aligned local-token similarity is a representation-space proxy and does not prove object identity, historical correctness, or plausible reconstruction.",
    "CLIP's 7x7 token grid is coarse and is used only as a complementary semantic localization signal.",
    "DINOv2 feature affinity is a diagnostic saliency proxy, not validated eye-tracking, attribution, or causal occlusion sensitivity.",
    "Category-conditioned interpretation does not imply that faces, anatomy, architecture, objects, or authentic brushwork were detected.",
    "The painterly representation metric compares DINOv2 patch-feature covariance and does not authenticate style, artist, or brushstrokes.",
    "SDXL evidence contains 24 technically validated completions from a predeclared 35-case bounded attempt and must not be interpreted as full model coverage.",
    "HINT contributes one deterministic primary candidate for every restoration-eligible controlled-300 case.",
    "Low semantic drift can coexist with consistently incorrect or historically unsupported restoration."
